# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
#
# Scoped USB device policy for the Android Auto receiver (task 29).
#
# SCOPE - narrow by construction. This file matches ONLY the qualified phone /
# AOA accessory identities on the qualified physical port path of the
# qualified host:
#
#   port path 1-2.1  (bus 1, root port 2 -> hub port 1; kernel sysfs name)
#     04e8:6860  Samsung Galaxy S24 Ultra, phone / MTP mode
#     18d1:2d00  Android Open Accessory (AOA) mode
#     18d1:2d01  Android Open Accessory mode + ADB (post-switch enumeration)
#
# The same ids on ANY OTHER port path do not match. There is no vendor-wide,
# class-wide or hub-wide rule here, no system-wide ModemManager disable, and
# no rule for the keyboard/mouse dongle, the Bluetooth radio, hubs or the
# usb-serial class at large: unrelated devices keep default udev and
# ModemManager policy.
#
# PORT CONSTRAINT: on this kernel (6.8.12-1021-tegra, verified with
# `udevadm info -a /sys/bus/usb/devices/1-2.1`) the USB device's kernel name
# IS the stable topology port path ("1-2.1"). KERNEL=="1-2.1" pins the device
# node exactly; KERNELS=="1-2.1" pins every descendant (interfaces, tty
# ports) of that one port. The alternative ATTR{devpath}=="2.1" is
# bus-relative ("2.1" without the bus prefix) and therefore ambiguous across
# the two USB buses on this target - it is deliberately NOT used.
#
# WHAT IS APPLIED (to the matched tree only):
#   1. ModemManager: ENV{ID_MM_DEVICE_IGNORE}="1" on exactly the matched
#      device tree (usb device + its interfaces + its tty ports). Without it
#      ModemManager probes the phone's CDC-ACM ports ("couldn't check support
#      for device ...: not supported by any plugin"). The id+port form here
#      follows ModemManager's own 77-mm-*-device-blacklist.rules convention
#      (ATTRS id match + ID_MM_DEVICE_IGNORE) plus the port constraint.
#      Every other device stays visible to ModemManager.
#   2. Receiver session access to the accessory bulk-pipe node
#      (/dev/bus/usb/BBB/DDD): GROUP="plugdev", MODE="0660",
#      TAG+="uaccess". plugdev + MODE 0660 + TAG uaccess is the project's
#      established Android-accessory ACL convention (tools/usb-policy/
#      README.md "Access control"); uaccess grants the active seat session
#      user and auto-revokes with the session; 0660 denies everyone else.
#      Least privilege: no MODE="0666", no world access, no class rules.
#
# NUMBERING: 70- runs after 50-udev-default.rules (so MODE/GROUP for these
# exact device nodes take effect) and before 73-seat-late.rules (so
# TAG+="uaccess" is registered before the uaccess builtin applies the ACL)
# and before the 77-/80- ModemManager rules. It cannot override later system
# rules.
#
# ROLLBACK: tools/usb-policy/rollback.sh restores the exact prior state.
# See tools/usb-policy/README.md ("Rollback").
#
# ROLLBACK DOC + ops: tools/usb-policy/README.md

# --- ModemManager: ignore exactly the matched device tree -----------------
KERNELS=="1-2.1", SUBSYSTEMS=="usb", ATTRS{idVendor}=="04e8", ATTRS{idProduct}=="6860", ENV{ID_MM_DEVICE_IGNORE}="1"
KERNELS=="1-2.1", SUBSYSTEMS=="usb", ATTRS{idVendor}=="18d1", ATTRS{idProduct}=="2d00", ENV{ID_MM_DEVICE_IGNORE}="1"
KERNELS=="1-2.1", SUBSYSTEMS=="usb", ATTRS{idVendor}=="18d1", ATTRS{idProduct}=="2d01", ENV{ID_MM_DEVICE_IGNORE}="1"

# --- Receiver session access to the accessory bulk-pipe node -------------
SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ENV{DEVTYPE}=="usb_device", KERNEL=="1-2.1", ATTR{idVendor}=="04e8", ATTR{idProduct}=="6860", GROUP="plugdev", MODE="0660", TAG+="uaccess"
SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ENV{DEVTYPE}=="usb_device", KERNEL=="1-2.1", ATTR{idVendor}=="18d1", ATTR{idProduct}=="2d00", GROUP="plugdev", MODE="0660", TAG+="uaccess"
SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ENV{DEVTYPE}=="usb_device", KERNEL=="1-2.1", ATTR{idVendor}=="18d1", ATTR{idProduct}=="2d01", GROUP="plugdev", MODE="0660", TAG+="uaccess"
